BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (14.1 CAN I USE TIME-TRAVEL ON WINDOWS OR MAC?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (NO. Time-Travel uses Linux kernel-specific interfaces:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (- inotify for filesystem events) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (- timerfd for periodic ticks) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (- rename\(\) atomicity guarantees \(POSIX\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 180.00 Td (- mkstemp for secure temporary files) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (There is no portability layer. It is Linux-only by design.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 132.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 120.00 Td (14.2 DOES IT WORK OVER NFS / SSHFS / NETWORK MOUNTS?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 108.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 96.00 Td (Partially. inotify DOES NOT work over NFS or SSHFS. The daemon will start ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (but won't receive events. The periodic rescan \(every 10 s\) will still ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 72.00 Td (capture changes, but with higher latency.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
33 0 obj
<< /Length 5187 >>
stream
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (For network directories, consider running the daemon on the server and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 768.00 Td (accessing the store remotely, or use a tool designed for network backup ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (\(BareSnap, Restic, Borg\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (14.3 HOW MUCH DISK SPACE DOES THE STORE NEED?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 696.00 Td (General rule: the store needs between 0.5x and 1x the size of the unique ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (data being tracked, depending on change frequency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (Factors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (- Delta encoding: small changes produce small deltas \(~20-30 bytes for a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (  line edit in a 600-byte file\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (- Full copies: very small files \(<~50 bytes\) are always stored as full ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 612.00 Td (  CREATE because deltas are larger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (- Compaction: collapses long delta chains into base + super-delta.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (- Binary files: photos, videos, compressed archives don't generate good ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td (  deltas; each version stores almost the full size.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (To check current usage:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (  timetravel status --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (14.4 CAN I BACKUP THE .TIMETRAVEL DIRECTORY?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (YES, but it's not recommended. The .timetravel directory contains all ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (history. Backing it up creates a circular dependency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (Better approach: backup the SOURCE files with a traditional tool \(BareSnap, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (rsync, tar\). The .timetravel store is a local undo buffer, not a backup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (14.5 WHAT HAPPENS IF THE DAEMON CRASHES?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (The store is NEVER left in a corrupt state:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (- Records are written atomically \(all or nothing\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (- Without fsync per record, some recent records might be lost on power ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (  loss, but existing records remain intact.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (- On restart, the daemon rebuilds its cache from disk and continues.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (- The PID file is cleaned on graceful exit; obsolete PIDs are detected via ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (  kill\(pid, 0\) and overwritten on new startup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (14.6 CAN TWO DAEMONS WATCH THE SAME DIRECTORY?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (NO. The second start detects the active daemon via the PID file and exits ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (with a message. This prevents duplicate records and conflicting cache states.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (Use timetravel stop --repo <dir> before starting a new instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (14.7 IS THERE ENCRYPTION?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 180.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 168.00 Td (NO. The store is plaintext under .timetravel/. For sensitive projects, place ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (the project directory inside a LUKS encrypted volume or use ecryptfs/fscrypt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 144.00 Td (Encryption is planned for a future version.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 120.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 108.00 Td (14.8 CAN I SYNC THE STORE TO ANOTHER MACHINE?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 96.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (Not natively. The store is a local undo buffer. For remote backup, use a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 72.00 Td (dedicated tool \(BareSnap with SSH, rsync, rclone\).) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
34 0 obj
<< /Length 4500 >>
stream
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 792.00 Td (You CAN rsync the .timetravel directory as a rudimentary sync mechanism, but ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (concurrent access from two machines is unsupported and will corrupt the store.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 744.00 Td (14.9 HOW DO I RESUME A SESSION?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (Simply restart the daemon over the same repository:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (  timetravel stop --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 696.00 Td (  timetravel start /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td (If the last .ttd is valid and hasn't exceeded the limit, the daemon will ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (continue writing to it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (To check session state:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (  timetravel status --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (14.10 CAN I SEE 100 DIFFS?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (Yes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (The recommended way is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (  timetravel dump <path> --repo <repo> --out /tmp/tt_dump --with-diff) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (Then:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (  find /tmp/tt_dump/diffs -name '*.diff' | sort | tail -n 100 | less) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (The practical limit isn't 100; it depends on available history, file sizes, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (and disk space for export.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (14.11 HOW DO I SEE THE CHANGE INTRODUCED BY A SPECIFIC REVISION?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (For revision N:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (  timetravel diff <path> --repo <repo> --from N-1 --to N) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (Example:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (  timetravel diff src/main.c --repo src --from 14 --to 15) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (For the first revision:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (  timetravel diff src/main.c --repo src --from 0 --to 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 300.00 Td (14.12 CAN I USE EXACT DATES FROM THE LOG?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (YES. Since v1.2, `undo --to` accepts exact timestamps in the format) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td ("YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" as shown in the log output.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (Example:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (  timetravel log src/main.c) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (  # Output shows: 2026-09-13 00:06:17  CREATE  ...  src/main.c) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (  timetravel undo src/main.c --to "2026-09-13 00:06:17" --repo src) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 180.00 Td (This restores the file to the exact state recorded at that second.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 144.00 Td (15. COMPARISON WITH OTHER TOOLS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 132.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 120.00 Td (+--------------------+-------------+----------+----------+----------+) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 108.00 Td (| Feature            | Time-Travel | git      | Restic   | BareSnap |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 96.00 Td (+--------------------+-------------+----------+----------+----------+) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (| Purpose            | Real-time   | Version  | Backup   | Backup   |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 72.00 Td (|                    | file undo   | control  |          |          |) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
