BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td (* git supports GPG signing but not repository encryption.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (Time-Travel occupies a unique niche: real-time per-file undo for active ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (development. It is NOT a backup tool. Use it alongside a proper backup ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (solution \(BareSnap, Restic, Borg\) for disaster recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (16. RESUMING A SESSION) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (Time-Travel automatically resumes the session when you restart the daemon ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (over the same repository.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (To stop and resume:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (./build/timetravel stop --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (./build/timetravel start /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (Behavior:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (- Looks for the last .ttd file inside .timetravel/) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (- If valid, not corrupt, not locked, and under 64 MB, continues writing to it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (- If missing, corrupt, locked, or over the limit, creates a new .ttd.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (Check session state:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (./build/timetravel status --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (View session files:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (ls -l /path/to/project/.timetravel/*.ttd) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (Important:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (There is no specific "session continue" command. The session resumes when ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (you run "start" again over the same repository.) Tj ET
